venv/
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
outputs/
.cache/
data/raw/*
# A `!` negation can't reach into a directory excluded by the pattern above unless
# the directory itself is re-included first — hence the un-ignore/re-ignore/
# un-ignore cascade below (see: git history "Force add test_results.csv", which
# worked around this same gitignore limitation instead of fixing it).
!data/raw/team-stats/
data/raw/team-stats/*
!data/raw/team-stats/team-records.csv
!data/raw/team-stats/team-payroll.csv
!data/raw/team-stats/coach.csv
!data/raw/master-stats/
data/raw/master-stats/*
!data/raw/master-stats/test_results.csv
!data/raw/master-stats/model_metadata.json
!data/raw/master-stats/master_df.csv
# Same cascade, same reason — backend/outputs/ is otherwise a gitignored build
# artifact directory (line 4 above), but these files are committed as source
# of truth for the API to read instead of live-fetching (Render's network
# can't reach stats.nba.com at all, confirmed across two regions, see
# backend/AGENTS.md's "Player ratings: refresh strategy"). All four are kept
# fresh by running the matching refresh_*.py script locally (where the same
# client works fine) and committing the result — the actual production
# strategy, not the .github/workflows/refresh-nba-data.yml schedule (scoped
# but not adopted; GitHub-hosted runners hit the same NBA.com block, so it's
# left in place as a dormant fallback, not relied on). Every other file under
# backend/outputs/ stays ignored.
!backend/outputs/
backend/outputs/*
!backend/outputs/player_power_rankings.json
!backend/outputs/team_style.json
!backend/outputs/player_projections.json
!backend/outputs/shot_heatmaps.json
